#Pipeline `|`: `a | f.` desugars to `f!a` — the LHS becomes the call's
 args list, exactly mirroring a direct `!` call. Multi-element list LHS
 spread across multiple positional slots, so functions that want the
 whole list as one binding should use the `___` variadic wildcard.#

first:{xs:___}(xs.0.)
rest:{xs:___}(xs.1~.)

#Single stage#
assert!((a b c) | first. a)
assert!((a b c) | rest. (b c))

#Multi-stage pipeline {left-associative}: a | f. | g. == g!f!a#
assert!(hello | split. | first. h)
assert!(hello | split. | len. 5)

#Whitespace around `|` is irrelevant#
assert!((1 2 3)|len. 3)
assert!((1 2 3)   |   first. 1)

#Pipeline accepts dotted callees and derefs#
chars:hello | split.
#The result is bound the usual way#
assert!(chars. | len. 5)

#A list-valued LHS feeds straight through as the call's args list#
assert!((x y z) | rest. (y z))

#Any expression that evaluates to a function value works as a stage.
 Here `getFn!first` calls a function which returns the first fn itself,
 which is then applied to the LHS by the pipe.#
getFn:{name:_}(name.?({first}(first.) {rest}(rest.) {len}(len.)))
assert!((a b c) | getFn!first a)
